# Feature branch workflow

Do not implement new features on `main`. Use a dedicated branch, then merge back.

1. Update local `main`: `git checkout main` && `git pull --ff-only origin main`.
2. Create and switch to `feature/<short-kebab-name>` (lowercase, hyphens, no spaces). Examples: `feature/alembic-migrations`, `feature/tenant-auth`.
3. Commit work only on that branch. Do not commit feature work to `main`.
4. When the feature is complete: push the branch, open a pull request into `main`, and merge. Delete the feature branch after a successful merge.
5. Docs-only or tiny rule tweaks that are not a product feature may use `chore/<name>` instead of `feature/<name>`, still not `main`.

Never force-push `main`. Never develop two unrelated features on the same branch.
